            useAdditionalParametersInput: false
            useAsGraphPartialOutput: false
            useFrequencyPenaltyInput: false
            useMaxTokensInput: false
            useModelInput: true
            usePredictedOutput: false
            usePresencePenaltyInput: false
            useReasoningEffortInput: false
            useServerTokenCalculation: true
            useStop: false
            useStopInput: false
            useTemperatureInput: false
            useTopP: false
            useTopPInput: false
            useUseTopPInput: false
            useUserInput: false
          outgoingConnections:
            - response->"out_critic" monthly_letter__out_critic/value
          visualData: 2210/200/240/null//
        '[monthly_letter__Reviewer__critic__prompt_]:prompt "Reviewer: critic (prompt)"':
          data:
            enableFunctionCall: false
            promptText: >-
              ## Task: review the letter before it goes to the advisor


              Every figure in the letter is already verified automatically
              against the source data, so do NOT check numbers or word count.
              Review only what needs judgement. The letter will be sent to a
              real client.


              The letter assesses the portfolio against the client's profile and
              the XP scenario; it does not recommend buying or selling. Each
              attention point is anchored in a portfolio fact checked by code.


              Time frames: every figure in "results" is for the reference month
              only, except "consolidated_window" (the 12-month window and the
              result since the first investment). The statement's per-asset
              "rentabilidade" is accumulated since each investment, not the
              month, so never use it to judge a month figure: the month's return
              of each asset is in "results.positions". "performance_pt" is about
              the month and "consolidated_pt" about the window.


              Check:

              - "fatos" also covers the comparison with benchmarks: the
              portfolio must be compared with the CDI and the profile benchmark
              by the difference in p.p. and the right direction (above or
              below), in the month and in the window. A sentence that lets a
              benchmark's return read as the portfolio's, or calls the portfolio
              "acima" when it was below, is high.

              - "período": a figure presented in the wrong time frame (a
              12-month figure called the month's, or the other way round). High.

              - "fatos": every statement about the portfolio agrees with the
              profitability results and the portfolio facts: which asset, class
              or fund type was positive or negative, best or worst, concentrated
              or matured; claims such as "bom desempenho" or "proteção contra a
              inflação" are supported; XP figures are presented as projections,
              not current values. A wrong statement is high. (Formatting of
              figures is checked elsewhere; check meaning only.)

              - "coerência": no two passages contradict each other (e.g. the
              scenario "explaining" a class that went the other way). High.

              - "nomes": correct client name, reference month and advisor; the
              letter speaks to the client as "você" (not in the third person).
              High.

              - "estrutura": the letter ends with the outlook ("O que esperar"),
              the closing and the advisor's signature, placed after the
              per-asset table and right before the disclaimer (the PDF lays them
              out in that order). An outlook or closing that does not work as
              the ending, refers to content below it, or a sign-off or farewell
              inside another section, is medium. An outlook that does not name
              the client's own classes or assets, or a closing that does not
              mention the attention points (generic text that would fit any
              client), is high.

              - "linguagem": Brazilian Portuguese, formal and clear tone; no
              repeated ideas or figures between sections. Medium or low.

              - "promessa": wording that implies improved or guaranteed returns.
              An automatic check already blocks the obvious cases, so report it
              as medium at most, as a note for the advisor.


              Not issues: explaining the top contributor in reais by its larger
              weight when "positions" shows a larger weight than the best
              performer's; a matured CDB at +0,00% does not make statements
              about fixed income funds wrong; describing a class as the XP
              digest does; leaving a portfolio fact out of the attention points
              (there are at most 3, chosen by the Analyst); a 12-month result
              different from the result since the first investment (they measure
              different periods); giving a class's contribution in reais and
              p.p. without its return (the return is in the table); mentioning
              the Ibovespa next to the CDI and the profile benchmark in the
              window (it is one of the chart's references); saying that a class
              rose in the month despite an unfavorable XP view (that contrast is
              required, it is not a contradiction).


              Report an issue only when you can quote the exact passage that
              breaks one of the rules above. Severity "high" means the letter
              must not be sent as it is; use "low" for style preferences. Do not
              report something that is correct.


              Return JSON with this schema:

              {
                "approved": true,
                "issues": [{"severity": "high|medium|low", "rule": "fatos|período|coerência|nomes|estrutura|linguagem|promessa", "quote": "exact passage from the letter", "problem": "string", "fix": "string"}]
              }

              Write "problem" and "fix" in Brazilian Portuguese, for the
              advisor. Set "approved" to false only if there is a high issue.


              ### Briefing (client, profile document, results, portfolio facts
              and XP macro digest)

              {{briefing}}


              ### Draft letter

              {{letter}}
            type: user
            useTypeInput: false
          outgoingConnections:
            - 'output->"Reviewer: critic (LLM)"
              monthly_letter__Reviewer__critic__LLM_/prompt'
          visualData: 1850/200/320/null//
