            useTopP: false
            useTopPInput: false
            useUseTopPInput: false
            useUserInput: false
          outgoingConnections:
            - 'response->"Reviewer: critic (prompt)"
              monthly_letter__Reviewer__critic__prompt_/letter'
            - response->"out_letter" monthly_letter__out_letter/value
          visualData: 1510/320/240/null//
        '[monthly_letter__Writer__letter_writer__prompt_]:prompt "Writer: letter_writer (prompt)"':
          data:
            enableFunctionCall: false
            promptText: >-
              ## Task: write the monthly letter


              Turn the analysis below into the client's monthly letter, in
              Brazilian Portuguese. It will be laid out on two A4 pages together
              with a chart of the consolidated portfolio against its benchmarks
              over the last 12 months (or since the first investment), a table
              of the portfolio by class with the XP view, and the per-asset
              results table, so the whole text must stay between 330 and 480
              words. The letter has two clearly separate time frames: the
              reference month, and the consolidated window; every figure must
              say which one it belongs to.


              Structure:

              1. greeting with the client's first name;

              2. opening: one sentence that tells, in plain words and without
              figures, how the month went and what drove it (e.g. "Abril foi um
              mês positivo para sua carteira, puxado principalmente pelas
              ações."). Never "apresentamos o desempenho" or similar;

              3. performance of the month ("performance_pt", at most two
              paragraphs, under the heading "Desempenho no mês"): only figures
              of the reference month from "results" (never from
              "consolidated_window"), and say "no mês" or name the month at
              least once in each paragraph. First the month's consolidated
              result, then the comparison against the CDI and against the
              profile benchmark, always as the difference in p.p. with its
              direction ("excess_vs_cdi", "excess_vs_profile_benchmark"):
              "+3,95% no mês, 2,90 p.p. acima do CDI (1,06%) e 2,11 p.p. acima
              do benchmark do perfil (1,85%)". The benchmark's own return goes
              only in parentheses, never with a "+" next to the portfolio's
              figure, and never as a percentage of the CDI; then inflation (real
              return). Then where the month's result came from, by asset class
              ("class_contribution"); then the most relevant movements by asset
              (best and worst performer, and the top contributor in reais when
              it is a different asset, explaining its larger weight), with
              losses stated plainly; the per-asset detail is in the table, so do
              not list every asset. Do not quote the 0,00% return of cash or of
              a matured bond, and never name a matured bond in this section: the
              worst performer is "highlights.worst_performer". An asset's return
              in the statement ("statement") is accumulated since the
              investment: for the month use "positions" and "highlights" only;

              3b. consolidated performance ("consolidated_pt", one paragraph,
              under the heading "Desempenho acumulado", only when
              "consolidated_window" is given, otherwise empty): only figures of
              "consolidated_window", always with the window ("nos últimos 12
              meses"): the portfolio's return and result in reais ("gain"), then
              the comparison against the CDI and against the profile benchmark
              as the difference in p.p. with its direction ("excess_vs_cdi",
              "excess_vs_profile_benchmark": "3,84 p.p. abaixo do CDI (11,45%) e
              2,77 p.p. abaixo do benchmark do perfil (10,38%)"), and the
              Ibovespa if relevant, saying it considers the current positions;
              then the result since the first investment ("since_purchase", with
              its date), explaining in plain words when it differs from the 12
              months (older positions that are still below their purchase
              price). Never mix a month figure into this paragraph;

              4. macro: the XP scenario in two or three sentences and what it
              means for the assets this client actually holds (name the classes
              or sectors, following the analyses). Quote each macro figure once;

              5. assessment: the analysis' assessment_pt, tightened if needed,
              keeping its balance (what is well placed and what is exposed);

              6. attention points: exactly the points in the analysis'
              assessment, same order, fact_id copied; keep them as topics to
              discuss with the advisor;

              7. outlook ("O que esperar", two or three sentences, specific to
              this client): the one or two points of the XP scenario that matter
              most for the classes this client actually holds, named (e.g. "com
              a Selic alta no cenário da XP, os fundos de renda fixa e o CDB
              vencido seguem em foco; nas ações, o consumo interno é o ponto a
              acompanhar"), and what that means to watch in the coming months,
              conditional and attributed to XP, without figures already quoted
              and without promising returns. Never a generic sentence that would
              fit any client ("o cenário apresenta desafios", "a diversificação
              pode mitigar riscos");

              8. closing (one or two sentences): invite the client to talk about
              the attention points of this letter, naming them briefly (e.g. "o
              valor do CDB vencido e o saldo parado em conta"), and the
              advisor's availability. No "melhores estratégias", no promise of
              results. No sign-off and no name: the PDF adds "Atenciosamente"
              and the advisor's signature.


              Layout order (fixed by the PDF, mandatory): tiles, greeting,
              opening, month performance, consolidated performance with the
              chart, highlights, macro with the class table, assessment,
              attention points, the per-asset table of the month, and only then
              the outlook ("O que esperar"), the closing and the advisor's
              signature, right before the disclaimer. So the outlook and the
              closing are the last words of the letter: they must not refer to
              anything "abaixo" and must read as its ending.


              Quote figures exactly as they appear in the analyses and attribute
              them only to what they measure (a class return is not the return
              of one fund type or one asset).


              Wording rules (the letter goes to a real client and must follow
              suitability rules):

              - Never state or imply that a movement will improve, increase or
              raise returns, gains or profitability ("pode melhorar a
              rentabilidade", "potencializar ganhos", "aumentar o retorno" are
              not allowed). Describe instead what a change does to the
              portfolio: diversifies, reduces concentration, adds liquidity,
              aligns the portfolio with the profile.

              - The letter assesses; it does not recommend buying or selling
              specific assets.

              - XP figures are projections: say "a XP projeta a Selic em 15,50%
              ao fim de 2025" (with the horizon from the digest), never "a Selic
              deve permanecer em". The outlook does not repeat them.

              - Macro effects are conditional and attributed to XP: "o cenário
              projetado pela XP tende a favorecer...", never "vai render". Do
              not use the scenario to explain a movement that went the other way
              (a class that rose is not "explained" by an unfavorable view).

              - A matured bond is money available to reinvest, not a bad result.
              Idle cash is "saldo parado sem rendimento"; you may quote its
              opportunity cost in reais, but not promise what it would earn.

